## Flags for the controller node. The launcher reads this file for the start
## commands only; `flzvm rpc` and `flzvm remote` read remote.vm.args.
## Customize: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here
##
## Every flag below is documented in docs/configuration.md under "Erlang VM
## arguments", and scripts/check-vm-args.sh fails when the two disagree.
## Override any of them with ERL_FLAGS in the environment, which is read after
## this file. ELIXIR_ERL_OPTIONS is read before it and cannot override one.

## A scheduler with no work stops spinning for it sooner. Measured against the
## default over paired rounds of the regression bench: 21% less CPU for the same
## run, with no throughput difference either window could resolve. `none` saves
## barely more (22%) and costs four times the setup latency, and spinning HARDER
## measured 33% more CPU and no faster. docs/configuration.md carries the table.
+sbwt short
+sbwtdcpu short
+sbwtdio short

## The ceiling on ports: plugin sockets, runner connections, distribution.
## Pinned because the default moves with the ERTS underneath (65 536 on the
## image's OTP 27, 1 048 576 on OTP 29), so the ceiling is a decision here
## rather than a property of whichever runtime was built in. The table is
## allocated up front at about 16 bytes a slot, so this also returns 15 MB of
## RSS on the larger default.
+Q 65536

## Already the default on OTP 27 and 29, pinned so a future ERTS cannot move it
## underneath the keepalive roster, which reads a monotonic epoch that is only
## well defined in this mode.
+C multi_time_warp

## Reclaiming refc binaries more aggressively is a memory-drift remedy, chosen
## against a measured series rather than set here. See
## docs/operations/memory_drift.md.

## Enable deployment without epmd
## (requires changing both vm.args and remote.vm.args)
##-start_epmd false -erl_epmd_port 6789 -dist_listen false
